 "blurb": "The screen cracks from a point of impact and breaks into shards of glass that turn and fall away from the middle outwards, showing the track below; the next clip's shards fly together into place. Unlike Shattered Glass, which stays cracked, this breaks the picture apart. Put it on both clips of a cut, or use Progress to key it by hand. The same seed always breaks the same way.",
